2	//! Request handlers (a.k.a. controllers) for EduGate Rustica.
3	//!
4	//! The handlers constitute the public, version-scoped REST surface of the
5	//! gateway.  Each handler orchestrates the flow below:
6	//! 1.  Metrics: increment call-counters & start latency timers.
7	//! 2.  Caching: short-circuit the request if a hot item lives in the cache.
8	//! 3.  Service layer: delegate the heavy lifting to an upstream micro-service
9	//!     abstraction (defined in `crate::services::*`).
10	//! 4.  Error mapping: translate domain/service errors into student-friendly
11	//!     HTTP responses (see `crate::errors::GatewayError`).
12	//!
13	//! NOTE: The file purposefully depends only on *traits* from the service and
14	//! cache layers.  Concrete implementations are wired together by `main.rs`
15	//! to facilitate unit-testing and allow dependency injection.
16	
