2	//! Response–caching subsystem for the EduGate Rustica API–Gateway.
3	//!
4	//! The gateway may sit behind thousands of mobile devices requesting
5	//! the same course catalog or leaderboard page.  Re-issuing those
6	//! expensive fan-out calls to downstream micro-services would be wasteful,
7	//! so we keep a small in-memory cache with a time-to-live (TTL).
8	//!
9	//! ## Design highlights
10	//!
11	//! * `CacheBackend` – an async trait abstracting concrete cache engines.
12	//!   – Default `InMemoryCache` (feature `in_memory_cache`, enabled by default).  
13	//!   – Optional `RedisCache` (feature `redis_cache`).
14	//! * Opt-in metrics collection (`CacheMetrics`) surfaced to the
15	//!   observability layer.
16	//! * API helpers such as `cache_or_compute` remove boilerplate from
17	//!   endpoint handlers.
18	//!
19	//! The implementation strives to stay dependency-light while still
20	//! demonstrating production patterns: feature flags, trait objects,
21	//! fine-grained locking, and structured error handling.
22	
